    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9659" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compŏsĭtūra</span></b>  (contr.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compostūra</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 22, 3</span></i>).
		ae, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				joining together</i>, <i>connection</i> (very
			rare, and only anteclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">olei, Cato, l. l.: oculorum,</span>”
				<i>a connection</i>, <i>commissure</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					4, 327</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of discourse, <i>conneclion</i>, <i>syntax</i>: partium
			orationis, Sinn. Capito ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 5,
				20, 2</span></i>.</div>
